            "created_at": "2025-09-28T01:19:30.343897+00:00",
            "notes": "Your round 1 ability can vastly differ depending on team and enemy comps. \n\n[Home Remedy](item_de68ba66-26d5-4136-a0c1-6396d3f1b0c7) is a safe option, because it will always benefit yourself. But is particularly good with teammates like [Orisa](hero_91644d44-1093-4f62-ac51-020975465e85), [Reinhardt](hero_a3b6ca2c-6cbd-43dc-bb78-a728e42fba49), [Cassidy](hero_3dd63854-7558-4344-86e4-b506f807129b), [Brigitte](hero_8d4e7c27-fb70-4694-9721-2ecf094ef84a), etc (basically characters that will be more grouped).\n\n[Venomous](item_594b0c79-5440-475c-b64c-c0295c46d735) is probably the best power if the enemy team has little or no cleanses (bonus if they have no shields either). The extra damage will be very impactful but less worth if the extra damage is being cleansed.\n\n[Time Out](item_34fc2f6c-ecd9-489e-98ca-d08f3eb2fac1) is also a great and underrated item, 50% slow is very strong. This item is great if your team is plannign to dive (liek [Winston](hero_a0ebe5ef-69a6-4a8f-9360-7b7fed8bce88)[Tracer](hero_bcc3aeb4-369e-4abb-b686-3234c169d37a) or [Genji](hero_31fd201d-2f46-41e4-b125-9fa9e55fed46)). They will be anti'd and slowed so they can't leave as your team dives them. Its also strong against some dive heroes like [Genji](hero_31fd201d-2f46-41e4-b125-9fa9e55fed46) since if they dive you it will make it easier to run away and trap them in your back line.\n\nChoose your first power from oen of these 3 based on team and enemy comps.",
